<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pisiri</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 738–717 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pisiri was the last king of Carchemish, the leading Neo-Hittite kingdom on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euphrates">Euphrates</a>. Long a tributary of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyria</a>, he was accused of plotting with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mita">Mita</a> (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/midas">Midas</a>) of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phrygia">Phrygia</a>, and in 717 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sargon-ii">Sargon II</a> deposed him, deported him with his family and made Carchemish an Assyrian province. His fall ended the last major Neo-Hittite state.</p></div>
